-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T14:05:58-08:00","id":32704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=32702#post32702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But those are my favorite threads *Puppy Dog Eyes*. We can take it elsewhere if you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be for the best *sigh* although be prepared that there is a good chance I'll visit it and tell you that I love Witchfinders :P<br /> <br /> (p.s- come on, convert your compacts into conspiracies! I know you want to *using Vice Projection*)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T14:34:50-08:00","id":32718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=32704#post32704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(p.s- come on, convert your compacts into conspiracies! I know you want to</div> </div> </div> </div> Nah, I'm kinda biased towards writing full Conspiracies so all of my Compacts are basically too niche to really work as Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The only one I can really think of working as a Conspiracy is The Reality Hackers. They would advance to a network trying to literally hi-jack The God Machine itself and take over reality for humanities benefit. Think of them as basically the humans from The Matrix, but without any prophecies or The One to do everything for them. They'd operate out of Demon like boltholes for their HQs and strange ships like the Nebuchadnezzar that can phase between reality and Twilight at the press of a button. Either way, they'd always have net access.<br /> <br /> I'd go so far as to port over the Cover system from Demon; but they can't use soul-pacts. Instead they use hi-jacked cover factories (the same ones the G-M uses for it's angels) and their'd be lots of hacking to build social security numbers, a Facebook profile and such to gain Cover XP. They can also spend Cover XP on Skills, Attributes and Merits that only apply for that cover and this is expected. Cover of 3+ is rare, most exist as implausible kickass martial artists in leather trenchcoats for one mission then are permanently abandoned.<br /> <br /> Their Endowments would be Apps, using the mechanics from Benediction and fluff wise, they're demon style Embeds coded as smartphone apps. Their second Endowment would be Hacks, where they take over Infersucture to do massive large scale workings. Permanently blinding the G-M to a large area (at least until it undoes it) or carving a whole town out of reality to create a large Bolthole (&quot;Zion&quot;, natch). This typically requires an operator sitting on their ship directing teams of hunters burst into Infrastructure with soldering irons, crowbars, laptops and start physically hacking.<br /> <br /> Their leader is an AI they built; their ultimate goal is to upload this AI into the G-M to replace it's current personality. If they're right that will create a utopia (think The Culture), if they're wrong. Meet the new boss, same as the old boss.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok... that's actually really really cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-18-2013, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T14:44:35-08:00","id":32725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=32718#post32718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nah, I'm kinda biased towards writing full Conspiracies so all of my Compacts are basically too niche to really work as Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> <br /> Ok... that's actually really really cool!</div> </div> </div> </div>*evil laughter* Even your mighty willpower can't withstand the Patron's powers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T17:20:33-08:00","id":32851,"title":"","content":"You know, about the other compacts, I kinda suspect the main canon God-Machine influenced one is the Null Mysteriis, due to that old standby of Lovecraftian fiction: the scholarly experiments accidentally contact something very alien, and changed the scholars.<br /> <br /> The subversion is that becoming stigmatic doesn't turn you into a crazy monster if you're sapient, it gives you psychic powers and an odd physical effect, but more importantly allows you to comprehend the God-Machine. To the Null Mysteriis, finding a being that literally embodies the logical, testable rules behind occult physics is the Holy Grail-they've proven that there's an internal logic to the madness of supernatural phenomenon, and they can begin to work on it.<br /> <br /> And thus, their Endowment: The science of using scientific means to affect supernaturals physics, and figuring out what Action A would result in Desired Outcome B.<br /> <br /> With fun things (for the table, not so much for the characters) happening if they screw up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T05:44:14-08:00","id":33097,"title":"","content":"To me that would defeat the purpose of the NM. The whole point about science is that it's the same no matter who you are, needing to get some crazy G-M powers first isn't science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T06:51:06-08:00","id":33146,"title":"","content":"thankfully, I'll still have some time to think about the Null Mysteriis, for I'm going to work by the order of the compacts- making the Long Night the next in the list. Any ideas for them? for now I think that their &quot;world changing event&quot; will be meeting an angel- you know, because of C&amp;C","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:09:48-08:00","id":33153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33097#post33097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me that would defeat the purpose of the NM. The whole point about science is that it's the same no matter who you are, needing to get some crazy G-M powers first isn't science.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing though. So is the occult physics of the God-Machine. Stigmata is ultimately secondary to their discovery of symbolism as a predictable, repeatable science. That some of them were mutated by exposure to an alien artificial intelligence is secondary to that, and most don't actually need to be stigmatic to utilize their discovery, nor do they want to. Hallucinations of a machine world mixed with paranoid delusions about being constantly threatened by some sort of construct angel, plus the bizarre physical effects, don't sound like they'd be worth accepting the abilities of some ancient machine to empower them (and of course, they think that making people stigmatic is all the artifact they discovered does-there's a large debate about whether it was meant for peaceful exploration of symbolic physics or creating warriors with Fortean abilities, let alone whether it was developed by a terrestrial civilization or not).<br /> <br /> And for the Long Night, I'd make what their &quot;angel&quot; was ambiguous. Much more thematic if you have to take their visitation on faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:34:15-08:00","id":33174,"title":"","content":"It would still be much thematically cleaner to have them find an alternative to becoming stigmatic. Though even then, the narrowing of their focus towards the God Machine dosen't sit right with me. NM study everything and their Conspiracy version should be the same rather than focusing around a single thing no matter how big.<br /> <br /> Besides the G-M isn't the holy grail. It's a lot easier to test and deduce about than magic, but it dosn't explain everything. Look at the Demon Stereotype on The Bound for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33146#post33146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thankfully, I'll still have some time to think about the Null Mysteriis, for I'm going to work by the order of the compacts- making the Long Night the next in the list. Any ideas for them? for now I think that their &quot;world changing event&quot; will be meeting an angel- you know, because of C&amp;C</div> </div> </div> </div>I might have to refresh my memory of C&amp;C.<br /> <br /> My idea for the LN would be something like apocalyptic doomsday fortresses. The Angel says that they don't need to help the apocalypse along any more, it's on it's way. Just wait a while. So the LN wait in their fortresses, safe from any monster who might end their life before they get to see Jesus again; and while they're waiting they go out and try to save souls. Endowment: Evangelism. It works like Agora Salve.<br /> <br /> Ok, I kinda prefer the Merciful creed; it's nice and unique in Hunter's thematic space. They'd still kill vampires and such, but only because the Vampire is in their way when they're trying to save the innocents locked up in the Vamp's basement.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T08:09:30-08:00","id":33203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33174#post33174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have to refresh my memory of C&amp;C.</div> </div> </div> </div>nothing important- just that they seelk after angels (which could look really strange) and could be fooled by creatures who look like one to do their bidding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T08:21:35-08:00","id":33211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33174#post33174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would still be much thematically cleaner to have them find an alternative to becoming stigmatic. Though even then, the narrowing of their focus towards the God Machine dosen't sit right with me. NM study everything and their Conspiracy version should be the same rather than focusing around a single thing no matter how big.<br /> <br /> Besides the G-M isn't the holy grail. It's a lot easier to test and deduce about than magic, but it dosn't explain everything. Look at the Demon Stereotype on The Bound for example</div> </div> </div> </div>I never suggested that they narrow their focus, only that they find something that's a good starting point for the real work, and provides context for Fortean phenomenon. The vampire is able to utilize blood to perform his powers, as symbolic physics allows him to transform his stolen blood into energy to accomplish those same feats.<br /> <br /> But that's a good point. They aren't necessarily stigmatics-they don't need to be, they've invented a work-around. Behold, the power of Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T08:36:02-08:00","id":33223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33211#post33211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never suggested that they narrow their focus, only that they find something that's a good starting point for the real work</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is what bugs me about the idea in a nut shell. The stuff they're doing now is as much &quot;the real work&quot; as anything they'll be doing in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T12:31:13-08:00","id":33340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33223#post33223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is what bugs me about the idea in a nut shell. The stuff they're doing now is as much &quot;the real work&quot; as anything they'll be doing in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh okay. I see the disconnect, and I completely agree.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to say the canon Null Mysteriis is sort of like the paranormal version of Victorian science, very smart people working with very little information, and coming up with theories that make perfect sense at the time and foreshadow greater discoveries to come, but in retrospect rather strange and silly (luminiferous aether comes to mind, as does homeopathy before germ theory), but dammit, they're trying!<br /> <br /> I imagine the conspiracy version of Null Mysteriis is something more like early-modern physics in the era of Einstein; they've developed the beginnings of the Theory of Everything, and are pointed in the right direction. More importantly, they've developed enough working knowledge to develop an Endowment, because they know the nitty-gritty of the more arcane physical laws of the nWoD (that these are generally under the header of Things Man Was Not Meant To Know, given the attitude of the Mysteriis, is probably viewed as &quot;Challenge accepted&quot;). I'm not denigrating what they do now, I'm just saying that they've only just begun their journey down the rabbit hole, and they suffer for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:54:08-08:00","id":33538,"title":"","content":"Now that I can agree with. It's just that, I don't think that the G-M provides that. In fact I think they'll have to make the progression from Victorian to modern for each major gameline separately. Some will be easier than others and yeah, the G-M will be among the easiest but studying it won't really say much about Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:58:01-08:00","id":33541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33538#post33538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I can agree with. It's just that, I don't think that the G-M provides that. In fact I think they'll have to make the progression from Victorian to modern for each major gameline separately. Some will be easier than others and yeah, the G-M will be among the easiest but studying it won't really say much about Sin-Eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T08:29:15-08:00","id":33881,"title":"","content":"So the conspiracy version of Null Mysteriis will be about finding the &quot;Theory of All&quot; which combine both mundane and supernatural scientific laws? sounds legit. I wonder how their Endowments would work..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T15:47:09-08:00","id":34641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=33881#post33881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the conspiracy version of Null Mysteriis will be about finding the &quot;Theory of All&quot; which combine both mundane and supernatural scientific laws? sounds legit. I wonder how their Endowments would work..</div> </div> </div> </div>Various experiments with things they've found, using mundane scientific equipment to play with various occult substances, whether inorganic or not.<br /> <br /> First, though, the Long Night. My guess it has to do with less formalized religious power than the Benedictions, more to do with general effects and Conditions, to keep with their evangelical grassroots theme.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T09:15:35-08:00","id":34957,"title":"","content":"The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood already has witches rumoured to be among its membership, so a witchcraft Endowment is a pretty natural fit, and doesn't even need a major catalyst to get there, just the knowledge spreading. Something neopagagan, probably: charms, wards, blessings of luck, healing, hiding, that sort of thing; Benediction probably makes the best model system-wise.<br /> <br /> Riffing off of what Leliel said, Null Mysteriis's Endowment could be modelled off of the path-based magical Endowments like the Rites du Cheval, but rather than spells, they're devices that utilise different supernatural energies, The &quot;paths&quot; would divide up by energies: scientific-sounding analogues of vitae, essence, sekhem, and pyros (or maybe swap pyros for aether),<br /> <br /> The Barrett Commission... the only way I could see them becoming a full-scale supernatural conspiracy would be to discover another such group infiltrating the halls of power, destroy it, and take its power for themselves. That would probably imply some sort of systematic magic, perhaps one connected with the idea of sacred kingship, which the Commission have sort of repurposed to the idea of patriotism rather than monarchy. Castigation might be a good model, in the sense of it granting you up to five of the powers associated with divinely ordained true kings.<br /> <br /> The Keepers of the Source... their worldview being what it is, I think they'd resist trying to develop an Endowment, certainly one that even looks like it might draw on places of power. The closest I can think is some sort of psychic power that draws on the user's own life energy.<br /> <br /> The Bear Lodge... their motive is basically to prove they can, which means that if they come regard the Vigil as sacred, it's the act of it, not the goals that they'll revere. So if that philosophy were to spread among them - that hunting is something sacred, to be undertaken in reverence to the act of it, they might start seeking out some form of hunting magic. Maybe communing with the genius loci of the places they move through to enhance their tracking and suchlike (a path for tracking, a path for survival, and a path for concealment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T09:57:40-08:00","id":34979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=34957#post34957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood already has witches rumoured to be among its membership, so a witchcraft Endowment is a pretty natural fit, and doesn't even need a major catalyst to get there, just the knowledge spreading. Something neopagagan, probably: charms, wards, blessings of luck, healing, hiding, that sort of thing; Benediction probably makes the best model system-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd be tempted to base it of Rites of Denial with literal maidens blood. I like making references out of names.<br /> <br /> That said; I've always liked the idea that the MBS always knew they had witches on the membership and most newbies tried to learn magic with little success. Not that you need an Awakening or anything unpredictable like that, rather it's just really really hard. Like PhD level mathematics. An Endowment would then be finding a series of rituals that anyone can do with little trouble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=34957#post34957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Barrett Commission... the only way I could see them becoming a full-scale supernatural conspiracy would be to discover another such group infiltrating the halls of power, destroy it, and take its power for themselves. That would probably imply some sort of systematic magic, perhaps one connected with the idea of sacred kingship, which the Commission have sort of repurposed to the idea of patriotism rather than monarchy. Castigation might be a good model, in the sense of it granting you up to five of the powers associated with divinely ordained true kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe base it on Unknown Armies style True Executives. Just like a True King is bound to the land, a True Executive is bound to an enterprise. They start with a goal and have powers to help make that goal reality and boost subordinates working towards the same goal. The Suits usually make money, the Quorum push polices and get elected, and the Five Stars win wars, all have goals based around keeping vampires out of Capitol Hill.<br /> <br /> However deep down, the idea of sacred kingship was that the king's responsibility was to look after the people. The sacred executive's only responsibility is to the bottom line. Feudalism failed utterly at being good for the common folk while capitalism is a big success for the bottom line; but ultimately is it better to do the right thing and fail or the wrong thing and succeed? I think this is a nice expansion of the Barrett Commission's dark side to an Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-23-2013, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T05:53:15-08:00","id":36882,"title":"","content":"so, it's Wednesday again, and you better prepare yourself for the Apocalypse- for here come the Long Night!<br /> <br /> <b>The Long Night</b><br /> <br /> The Long Night are diverse. They've always been. However, one thing has always united them- the End of Times. Suffering in the Tribulation until the Rapture would come. The Apocalypse, when Jesus would return and the righteous would be saved from this world of darkness. The hunters of the Long Night are united with their faith, and that faith has led them to try and save the souls of others or fighting the monsters with zealously. <br /> <br /> In order to help the Apocalypse to come, the faithful hunters of the Long Night has did their best to proof their righteousness- and finally, after years of work, their efforts has finally paid off. It has all started in the 1.7.13- which is a very important date. during that time, three among the most charismatic leaders of the compact has fallen in their place, covered with white halo while in coma. The event has made the members of the compact start to panic, not sure if it is a sign for the power of Satan or God, with the number 7 stand against the 13. Two days later, another prominent member has fallen into the same state, and the panic has turned into an hysteria. Four days later, another three has fallen- and the faithful hunter couldn't miss the numerological importance. With seven leaders in a coma on the 7.7.13, it truly looked like it was a sign.<br /> <br /> The fear inside the compact has swelled with each and every day, not sure what was supposed to happen now- are they attacked by the forces of Hell? Is it the Rapture? And if it is the Rapture, why aren't all of them join their leaders? Are they don't righteous enough? Those thoughts has made the more zealot members of the compact to start act a bit.. crazy. Some has started to attack the monsters without stopping, and many members were lost during that time. Others have committed mass ritual suicide, believing that this way they would reach Heaven. The Merciful, who were the most stable creed, tried to do their best to keep things under control, but at each day which passed the panic spread more and more.<br /> <br /> At the 13.7.13, happened a thing which turned the hysteria into madness- seven more members of the compacts has fallen. doubling the number of leaders in coma into 14. Many hunters, believing that the End is near at every moment, has bonded together for suicide missions against vampires, shifters and witches. The rest of the hunters, however, decided on the a different way to deal with it. The remaining leaders of the compact has gathered the members together with their fallen leaders and told them to pray the whole night. The members, each with his own faith and way, has joined together and prayed that may the world become better thanks to the coming of the Christ and that may the Apocalypse will come and pass, finally purifying the darkness.<br /> <br /> And when the clock hit midnight, another sign has came.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, a great white light has filled the room, shining like a new sun- and behind the light, all of those present could feel a.. presence. Something they couldn't see with their mortal eyes, but their soul has felt. And after the light passed, the 14 sleeping members of the compact has awakened. They told the other members that they have done well, for this was a trial by God himself to see if they are truly righteous enough to serve as a path to the Christ- this was their Long Night. Their faith has opened the gate, and as long as they keep their faith, the Rapture would come. Also, the leaders has told them a story about their revelation- that while they slept, an angel has came to them and told them they have the potential to save the souls of others, and that it awakened that potential in them. They have became a bastion of their faith, and as such those who will become part of the Long Night will be saved when the fires of God would clean the world.<br /> <br /> The angel also said that they still have one mission in order to usher the Apocalypse- they must find the 147 saviors of humanity, which are hidden in the world. Once they'll join, Jesus would finally return. In order to proof its words, the angel promised that another sign would show in the next day. When the members asked about which sign will it be, the leaders replied that the angel told them they would know. When the members asked how the angel looked like, the members simply started to cry, telling them it was &quot;out of this world&quot;.<br /> <br /> When the sun rose, the members of the Long Night has discovered the sign the angel has promised. Outside of the place where they prayed there were 13 burned corpses of vampires. The bloodsuckers has found out that the source of the wild attacks lately has came from the Long Night, and went to get rid of them- and the light of the angel has burned them to ash. Apparently, the date truly had a numerological importance- 14.7.13. 7 members has fallen in the 7th, and the light of the 14 awakening members has burned the 13 creatures of darkness. After that, the members has started with their mission to seek and save as many souls as possible before the coming of the Apocalypse while searching after the 147 hidden saviors. During their attempt to requite new members, they discovered that the angel truly blessed them with the ability to saver others- their tongues now carried a mystic power, and people had to listen to their words.<br /> <br /> Thanks to the angelic gift, their numbers grew, and with it their knowledge and understanding. While they remained diverse as always, they were united under a new mission and the vision of the angel, under the supervision of the 14 Prophets, as now those who has seen the face of the angel were called. While each had his own agenda and way, their united revelation has bonded them together in bonds which are deeper of blood. That made the members start to fear from what would happen if one of the 14 would die, but the Prophets has promised them that they don't need to worry. If it meant that another prophet will join once one would fall, that the Jesus would come before any of them would die or something else entirely is, currently, unknown.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- Instead of Evangelism as a specialty, you get it as an Endowment- or, as the members of the Long Night prefer to call it, Blessed Speech<br /> 000- same<br /> 00000- same<br /> <br /> <b>Endowment: Blessed Speech</b> (0-00000, special)<br /> <br /> The angel said it awakened their ability to save others, and it meant so they could do it with words alone. Blessed Speech is an Endowment which allow the members of the Long Night to convince, scare and even save those whom listen to them. Each Blessed Speech is based around a single Condition (see GMC rules update), and is rated from 1 to 5. The Endowment is built around rolling Persuasion while talking with the target. The target doesn't need to try and listen to the hunter, or even to understand what he says- so the hunter can talk with English to someone who only understand Spanish, or even a vampire which has awakened after the sleep of the thousand years- this is the gift of their angel. The only limitation is that the target must be able to hear the hunter (meaning, deaf people are not a valid target) and that the target must have a mostly human mind (so abyssal entities, spirits, animals and others inhumane things are not a valid targets. Humans, vampires, werewolves and witches are). If there is more than one target which could hear them, the hunter can decided who to effect with his Speech and who not to effect- the target just feels that the words are directed to her and not to the others. The Speech must be live, so recording the Speech won't keep the effect.<br /> <br /> The use of the Endowment is otherwise identical to the use of Persuasion, with the hunter add a number of dices equal to his number of dots in the chosen Blessed Speech. A dramatic failure mean that not only means that the attempt has failed, but that the hunter couldn't believe that it failed, losing some of his faith in himself- together with a Willpower point. A success means that the hunter has managed to convince the target with his holy words- and force on her the chosen Condition. The effect lasts for number of hours equal to the number of dots in the chosen Blessed Speech. And Exceptional Success means that the Condition effects for number of <i>days</i> equal to their dots in their chosen speech. Most people who are target by an exceptional success are usually easy to be requited by the Long Night, and are pretty surprise to discover few days later to the conspiracy &quot;for their own sake&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T10:02:23-08:00","id":36952,"title":"","content":"*pbbt*<br /> <br /> Weaponized evangelism!<br /> <br /> Why does this make so much sense, and is yet so hilarious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T10:31:31-08:00","id":36963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=36952#post36952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*pbbt*<br /> <br /> Weaponized evangelism!<br /> <br /> Why does this make so much sense, and is yet so hilarious?</div> </div> </div> </div>hey, that's the only thing I could think about! Those are quick and dirty rules, after all, and I didn't wanted to say &quot;just use Benedictions under a different name&quot;. It was also inspired from one of the possessed vestments (the one which kills anyone who can hear anyone who hear the the possessed).<br /> <br /> Anyway, the next compact is the Loyalists, with NM after them (yay! one less compact to work on!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T22:27:00-08:00","id":37709,"title":"","content":"Interesting! I like the idea, and look forward to more write-ups.<br /> <br /> Some questions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=32430#post32430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Ashwood Abbey</b><br /> <br /> .....................................<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- you have just signed your contract and joined the Abbey. You are now able to buy dots in Vice Projection. You also get 1 dot Resources from the Abbey to help you focus on the hunt<br /> 000- The dots in the Resources rise to 2 dots and you get the safe house benefit (see H:tV core book)<br /> 00000- Resources rise to 3 and you get the same benefit as given in H:tV core book.<br /> <br /> <b>Endowment: Vice Projection (0-00000, special)</b><br /> <br /> Once a new member joins the Abbey, he or she sign a contract. In exchange for the conditions in the contract, the member gets a special ability- the power to sense the passions and hidden desires of others- and influence them.<br /> <br /> Each Vice Projection is focused around a single Vice (see the GMC rules update for details).<b>(1)</b> Having one dot in it allows you to sense if the Vice of your target is the same as the Vice of the Projection after 30 seconds of talking with the target or expanding one Willpower point. This Require rolling Empathy, with adding number of dices as equal to your dots in the Vice Projection.<b>(2)</b><br /> <br /> After doing so, there are two options. First, if the target's Vice is not the same as the Vice Projection, you can try to change it. This requires around a full minute of talking with the target or expanding 2 Willpower points, and than rolling (Persuasion + Vice Projection).<b>(3)</b> The Dramatic Failure is the same of a failed Persuasion roll, with a success meaning that you managed to change the target's Vice to the desired one for 10*(Vice Projection dots) minutes. Exceptional success means that the duration is doubled.<br /> <br /> After the Vice has changed, or if there was no need to change the Vice, the fun can finally begin. After talking with the target for 5 minutes<b>(4)</b> or expanding 3 points of Willpower, you can force the target to indulge her Vice. There are two ways to use that power- the first to force the target to do a single act which is supposed to fulfill her Vice, and after that the effect of the Endowment is over. This is called &quot;Focused Projection&quot;. The other form is more of an investment- for number of minutes equal to 10*(Vice Projection) the target need to fight an urge to fulfill her Vice. This is represented by rolling(Resolve + Composure) against the (Vice Projection + Manipulation) of the user.<b>(5)</b> Each Willpower point which was supposed to be given to the target for fulfilling her Vice while under the effect of the Projection is instead given to the user of the Endowment. This is called &quot;Free Projection&quot;.<br /> <br /> In order to project a Vice the user must roll (Vice Projection + Manipulation) against the target's (Resolve + Composure). Dramatic Failure means that the target is now immune to any further attempts to manipulate their Vice for a number of minutes equal to 10*(Willpower Dots). Exceptional Success for a &quot;Free Projection&quot; means the time on which the target is effected is doubled and she suffer from -2 modifier to try and resist the urge to fulfill the Vice. Exceptional success in the &quot;Focused Projection&quot; means that the target also suffer from the effects of a &quot;Free Projection&quot; after fulfilling the act for number of minutes equal to 5*(Vice Projection).<b>(6)</b><br /> <br /> This power can not be used against inhuman creatures which are not originate from humans (mages, ghosts, sin eaters, prometheans, etc are valid targets. Spirits, strixs, and angels are not). If the target lack a Vice but originate from an human (like vampires post Blood and Smoke) the user may try to force the target to act upon the Vice, but he needs at least 3 Dots in the Vice Projection and suffer -3 modifiers for all rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Does this mean you can take this Endowment multiple times, each time keyed to a specific Vice, or each dot adds another Vice you can 'scan' for? If you have at least one dot in four of them, (or four dots, if the second of the question I just asked) would you need to take 30 seconds for each one, or does one check let you know which of the four (or none of the four) Vices is the target's?<br /> <br /> 2) Wouldn't this roll be Wits + Empathy + Vice Projection? I'd also think that you subtract or resist with the target's Composure if they are &quot;on guard&quot;, playing a part, or otherwise are suspicious. What Specializations would you say would help? &quot;Reading People&quot; and &quot;Psychoanalysis&quot; come to mind.<br /> <br /> 3) Typically you'd add an Attribute to a roll. So for here, Manipulation + Persuasion + Vice Projection, again, either subtracting or vs. the target's Composure.<br /> <br /> 4) Wouldn't this cut into the time for the changed Vice?<br /> <br /> 5) How often? Once a minute? Once a round?<br /> <br /> 6) From the normal effects of &quot;Free Projection&quot;, or the Exceptional Success result of &quot;Free Projection&quot;, since this is an Exceptional Success?<br /> <br /> Finally, what happens if you try to use this in combat? I'm imagining someone taking Vice Projection: Individuality, and trying to use this to get someone to rebel against someone who's giving them orders (Think Luke Skywalker/Darth Vader in Return of the Jedi) Does it last for 10*(Vice Projection) rounds, instead of minutes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T23:03:19-08:00","id":37723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=36882#post36882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Long Night</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So, Presence + Persuasion + Blessed Speech, subtracting or contesting with the target's Resolve? I would also ask what sets the 147 &quot;saviors&quot; apart from the other recruits, though like what the Patron gets from the signatories for the Abbey I would assume this is up to the individual Storytellers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T14:11:55-08:00","id":38002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=37709#post37709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! I like the idea, and look forward to more write-ups.<br /> <br /> Some questions:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1) Does this mean you can take this Endowment multiple times, each time keyed to a specific Vice, or each dot adds another Vice you can 'scan' for? If you have at least one dot in four of them, (or four dots, if the second of the question I just asked) would you need to take 30 seconds for each one, or does one check let you know which of the four (or none of the four) Vices is the target's?<br /> <br /> 2) Wouldn't this roll be Wits + Empathy + Vice Projection? I'd also think that you subtract or resist with the target's Composure if they are &quot;on guard&quot;, playing a part, or otherwise are suspicious. What Specializations would you say would help? &quot;Reading People&quot; and &quot;Psychoanalysis&quot; come to mind.<br /> <br /> 3) Typically you'd add an Attribute to a roll. So for here, Manipulation + Persuasion + Vice Projection, again, either subtracting or vs. the target's Composure.<br /> <br /> 4) Wouldn't this cut into the time for the changed Vice?<br /> <br /> 5) How often? Once a minute? Once a round?<br /> <br /> 6) From the normal effects of &quot;Free Projection&quot;, or the Exceptional Success result of &quot;Free Projection&quot;, since this is an Exceptional Success?<br /> <br /> Finally, what happens if you try to use this in combat? I'm imagining someone taking Vice Projection: Individuality, and trying to use this to get someone to rebel against someone who's giving them orders (Think Luke Skywalker/Darth Vader in Return of the Jedi) Does it last for 10*(Vice Projection) rounds, instead of minutes?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) yes, each Vice projection is a separate endowment which is based around a single Vice (in a similar way that each Blessed Speech is based around a single condition, BTW), and you'll need 30 seconds per Vice you scan.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, this is the roll- and using Composure to resist makes sense, and so does the specializations.<br /> <br /> 3) I think that vs Composure is makes more sense<br /> <br /> 4) yes<br /> <br /> 5) It is not determined by time- it is just that when such temptation rises, the target must role in order to avoid indulging the Vice. For example, if someone has the Vice of Individuality, they'll have to role every time someone gives them orders or tries to force them to become &quot;part of the herd&quot;<br /> <br /> 6) Normal effect. While it is an Exceptional Successes, I don't think it should be doubled :P<br /> <br /> 7) Yes, this is supposed to be able to be used in battle (which is why you could also use WP instead of talking). Free Projection will still last for minutes, because it simply tempts the target to indulge the Vice (with some help). In battle, it is better to use the Focused Projection (so instead to tempting the target to rebel, you force it to rebel)<br /> <br /> Edit- had a delay for a while.. finally got it *blush*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 12-31-2013, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T14:13:33-08:00","id":38003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/32396-moving-up-in-the-tiers-compacts-into-conspiracies?p=37723#post37723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Presence + Persuasion + Blessed Speech, subtracting or contesting with the target's Resolve? I would also ask what sets the 147 &quot;saviors&quot; apart from the other recruits, though like what the Patron gets from the signatories for the Abbey I would assume this is up to the individual Storytellers.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep, this is the roll.<br /> <br /> And yes, both the Angel and the &quot;saviors&quot; from the Long Night and the Patron are left to the Storyteller- although I have an head canon for them (with the Patron as the most detailed one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:35:40-08:00","id":40109,"title":"","content":"so- tomorrow I'm posting the Loyalists, and there are few things I'm not sure about..<br /> <br /> For now, the idea is going to involve the death of the 3 Old Men and making them into ghosts (unable to let go of their past sins). Also, there is a chance ghosts would turn up to be dominant in the Loyalists as an information source. I'm also don't sure about their Endowment, for they have many occult rituals and relics already. I'm thinking about focusing their Endowment around either information searching (some sort of divination/ scrying) or something with the Rmohalans...<br /> <br /> and last minute advices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:59:56-08:00","id":40118,"title":"","content":"Information overarching, definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T06:19:49-08:00","id":40482,"title":"","content":"<b>The Loyalists of Thule</b><br /> <br /> In the times they were a compact, all of the Loyalists had one thing in common- all of them have messed up, and they dedicated all of their life in order to repay for their past sins. Their search after hidden secret, obscure knowledge and occult relics was all made in order to repair the damage they once did. They harmed the world because of occult, and now they are going to fix things with occult. That simple. That ideology has, more or less, stayed the same when they turned into a conspiracy- just that now, they debt doesn't end with their life.<br /> <br /> It has all started with a vampire assault. The bloodsuckers has knew about the existence of the compact, and while they were annoying they didn't saw them as a real threat. After all, they were just a group of foolish mortals who knew too much for their own good. Eventually, the curiosity will kill the cat, and they didn't had the urge to don its job for it. That attitude has changed when one of the Loyalists' hunters has managed to break into one of the high ranked vampires' haven and still a list of above 30 princes, together with their location and personal retainers. That was too much for the vampires to bear, and so they decided to get rid of them in the same way you kill a snake- you cut off its head.<br /> <br /> It took them a while, but they eventually found the so called leaders of the compact- The Three Old Men. After tracking down the hunter and the list before he could do some real damage, they broke into the Old Men' house and murdered them all, mutilating their bodies and wrote with their blood &quot;Stay Away From Our Secrets&quot;. They thought it was enough for the rest of the compact to &quot;take the hint&quot; and left, assuming that the compact will descend into chaos without its leaders and may even break apart.<br /> <br /> That showed how little they knew about the Loyalists.<br /> <br /> The Three Old Men were, after all, old. They prepared for their death long time ago. Even with them gone, the compact should have still worked without them. They were symbols more than leaders, and while their death would harm the Compact's morale, the Loyalists should just keep working as usual. Nothing was supposed to change.<br /> <br /> Only that things didn't happened as they should have.<br /> <br /> When they were torn apart by their killers, they were scared- but not of dying. They were scared from their fate after death. They felt that they didn't fulfilled their debt, and that there was so much knowledge they didn't found, too sins they couldn't repay for. That, and the violence of their death, didn't let them move on, trapping them as ghosts in the physical world. However, something strange has happened- unlike most of the ghosts, they retained their knowledge and personality. They weren't just an hollow shell. They were aware- and their fetter was no other than the Loyalists themselves.<br /> <br /> That wide fetter has made another abnormality in their state- while they retained their spiritual body, their mind has turned into a network of information, connection to the subconscious of all of the members of the compact. Through this network, they managed to commune with all of the hunters and give them the details about what happened. That also allowed them to share their experience and supervise the compact directly. That network allowed them to make sure that no information will ever be lost, and so secret will be forgotten.<br /> <br /> It also meant that the Three Old Men had a direct access to each of the hunter's thought's allowing them to monitor potential betrayal and any secret they tried to hide from the rest of the Loyalists- but it is for a good cause, right?<br /> <br /> Of course, three lost souls aren't enough to monitor all of the compact- but the network had another side effect. The Loyalists couldn't move on. Once they died, they would be absorbed by the network and serve it as another &quot;computing space&quot;, allowing to monitor more members and contain more information. Those souls didn't had their personality like the Three Old Men had, but they didn't needed it. The network got a major boost to its power when, under the directions of the Old Men, the Loyalists added ghosts of the Rmoahals to the network, which was named as the Archive for sort.<br /> <br /> After having that much information, they Loyalists discovered they could the Archive to do great and terrible things- like, predicting future events through calculating. That allowed them to grow in power and influence by gaining money from the stock market and finding good places to invest their money on. They managed to track down more future members- people who messed up. And eventually, they claimed their status as a conspiracy- and this time, the vampires no one to target. You can't cut the head of an headless snake.<br /> <br /> Now, death is not the end for the Loyalists. There is no end for one's sins. There is only trying to repay for your mistakes- for ever and ever.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- same as the core, and you can spend merit points of the Loyalist's Endowment- Das Archiv: Spezialit\u00e4t<br /> 000- same as H:tV core. You can also spend merit points on Das Archiv: Verzauberung<br /> 00000- Your knowledge is appreciated by the Old Men and your members, and you get help in order to help you with your projects. You get Staff for 3 dots. You can also spend merit points on Das Archiv: Korrespondenz.<br /> <br /> <b>Endowment: Das Archiv</b> (0-00000, special)<br /> <br /> Das Archiv, or &quot;the Archive&quot;, was once the name of a secret collection of information kept by the Three Old Men. After their death and the creation of the &quot;ghost network&quot;, the name was instead given to the collective conscious of all of the dead members of the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> The Das Archiv has a number of functions, with each is bought as a separate 1-5 merit. Unlike most Endowments, each function is limited by the status to the member, which means that an hunter may not use some of the effects of Das Archiv unless his status is high enough. That was made by the Three Old Men in order to make sure no one will get information he shouldn't, and than will only make even more mess.<br /> <br /> The first is Spezialit\u00e4t, or &quot;specialty&quot;. By spending a willpower point and deciding on a certain skill, the hunter can tune into the collective conscious of the dead members in order to get strength. Next time he'll role that skill, he could add a number of dice equal to his dots at Das Archiv: Spezialit\u00e4t. The Loyalist can prepare only 1 such skill bonus at a time.<br /> <br /> The second effect is called Verzauberung, or &quot;enchantment&quot;. That power allows the hunter to mimic any Dread Power he saw by creating some sort of an occult ceremony- thanks to the information gained from the Rmoahals. The ritual takes 6-(dots in Verzauberung) minutes, and than the Loyalists rolls Occult + Verzauberung (which could be magnified thanks to Spezialit\u00e4t). Dramatic failure means that not only that the ritual failed, but that the hunter lost control over the occult energies- expressed with a bashing damage per dot of Verzauberung. Exceptional success means that not only that the ritual worked, but that the hunter understood the structure of the ritual, getting a +2 modifier for the next time he'll use Verzauberung. They hunter can't make a ritual for a Dread Power which its dot rating is higher than his dots in Verzauberung.<br /> <br /> The last function is called Korrespondenz, or &quot;correspondence&quot;. That function relays on the connections between the different hunters through the Archiv. For each dot in Korrespondenz the hunter have a connection with another member of the conspiracy he met, and by expanding a Willpower point they can talk with the other hunter for another minute. That connection may not be used if another Hunter is already talking with the target, and the Willpower point isn't expended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T06:21:08-08:00","id":40483,"title":"","content":"Next week- the Null Mysteriis. Any ideas about their &quot;changing event&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T10:35:09-08:00","id":44978,"title":"","content":"<b>Null Mysteriis</b><br /> <br /> Among the many compacts, the ORAS is one of the most organized groups. Their rigid hierarchy and structure are among the best available for a tier 2 group. However, being in the Null Mysteriis is also very expansive, and with so much money invested simply in order to allow the organization to exist, the option of growing and becoming a full scale conspiracy seemed improbable. Add that with the internal strives between the different Theories (with some members on the verge of committing murder), and you'll discover that their teamwork is also lacking and that rising in power is even less possible.<br /> <br /> However, when two fight the third always wins, and the turning point of the organization has came from two different directions.<br /> <br /> The first turning point was what the Cataclysmicists called the &quot;Pressure Release&quot;. Suddenly, without warning, clouds has started to gather, heralding the coming of great lightning storms- in the middle of the summer. While most of the people were in awe from the phenomena and the weathermen tried to search after an explanation, the Null Mysteriis has tried to find a rational way to think about the problem. According to all indicators, the storm wasn't natural- but the disagreement was in how it happened. The Rationals claimed that it may be some manifestation of electromagnetic field generated by some supernatural energy source. The Open Minded claimed that beings from other dimensions may effect the world. That, of course, made the two groups to start fight. Finally, the Cataclysmicists rose up and told everyone to shut up- backing their words with guns (&quot;so HERE is where all of the money went...&quot;)<br /> <br /> The Cataclysmicists told the rest of the compact that the time to watch is over- and now is the time to actually DO things. They told hem to sit together and start search for a way to stop that storm. That was when Alexander Watt had enough and started laughing, asking them if they were going to shot them if they won't cooperate. That was when the Cataclysmicists lowerd their guns and said &quot;No- but you won't be able to access our specially made shelters when the storm will strike&quot;.<br /> <br /> That was enough for both the Rationals and Open Minded to swallow their pride and start working together- after all, that course of action was the most logical thing to do. Working together for the first time after long years of being apart, the different members of the ORAS has managed to built a theory which was, more or less, accepted on most of the members. According to it, there are invisible phenomena which can't be seen, and there is a possibility for the existence of other dimensions (the Rationals didn't agreed to use the word &quot;spirit&quot; directly). Apparently, those phenomena react to the electromagnetic field generated by human mind (the Rationalists didn't agreed to use &quot;soul&quot; or &quot;emotions&quot;), and react accordingly. In an addition, those phenomena may effect the physical world by reacting to the human mind and effect it according to the type of electromagnetic field which has drawn them. That storm, which was &quot;radiating Essence&quot; according to the Open Minded connection with &quot;shamans and hedge witches&quot;, was apparently the creation of such &quot;spiritual phenomena&quot; , and that it was created from &quot;negative mind patterns&quot;, so the only way to solve the problem was by generating &quot;positive mind patterns&quot;.<br /> <br /> And here was the problem- how could the Null Mysteriis make enough people happy?<br /> <br /> That was the second turning point. Under the guidance of the Cataclysmicists, the different Theories has worked together in order to built a machine which would feed the so called &quot;Essence&quot; in the human mind, amplify it and send it into the storm. Sure, it may sound impossible, but after gathering all of their information together and removing anything which was clearly wrong from both sides, the Null Mysteriis has managed (after several failures and few fried mice) to built a machine which was able to drain Essence from a Loci, move it into a human mind and project it to the storm. Unbelievably, the machine worked, and in a few hours the storm vanished without trace, leaving confused weathermen and happy Cataclysmicists.<br /> <br /> After that, the compact has decided it had the means to truly understand how the supernatural worked- after all, if they were able to built a machine which works on supernatural energy, what could be the limit for their abilities? They could solve the energy crises! They could be rich! But this is not the way of the Null Mysteriis. They should work on theories, not physical products. However, there are people- both mundane and supernatural- which are interested in such products, and by using the contacts of the Open Minded, the ORAS has presented the more scientific minded among those to invest in them financially while they would work on new products and inventions. While not all of them agreed, few of them (a number of vampires from an organization called &quot;Ordo Dracul&quot;, a group of technologically based lycanthropes and some mages with pseudo- scientific belives) has agreed to help them. With that money, the Null Mysteriis were able to start and search more actively after potential members while learning new information about the certain energies which exist in the supernatural world.<br /> <br /> During that research, they have came into a conclusion- in the same way that there are no real &quot;energy types&quot; but simply different forms of energy, and that all of the existing forces should become eventually into a single force, there should also be a way to unite the different energies- Mana, Essence, Vitae, etc- into a single kind of pure, supernatural power. That means that, in a way, all of the supernatural phenomena are originated from a single source, and are actually the same. That &quot;Supernatural Theory of One&quot; is the new mission of the Null Mysteriis. Those inventions which work on supernatural power? Oh, those are just financial income source. No, they don't prepare for another apocalypse. yep, this is a gun- don't touch it! You know how much Mana was invested in order to make that one?<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- you get access to the Energetic Theories endowment<br /> 000- Allies is the same, while the Contacts is changed into one supernatural creature from a scientific organization<br /> 00000- same<br /> <br /> <b>Endowment: Energetic Theories</b> (0-00000, special)<br /> <br /> this endowment represent the knowledge of the Null Mysteriis on the different supernatural energies and the ways to manipulate them. Sure, the ORAS is seeking after their own &quot;Theory of One&quot;, but until then they must relay on working with &quot;lesser forms of energy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Each Energetic Theory is based around a single &quot;energy type&quot;. &quot;Energy type&quot; is any kind of supernatural energy, like Essence, Mana/ Source, Vitae, Glamor and other weird energies. Each such energy is rated from 1-5, and that rating allows a number of functions.<br /> <br /> First, is the theoretical understanding of the subject. Anytime an hunter needs to investigate a subject which works on the energy type he has knowledge in, he may add his dots in the appropriate Energetic Theory to the role. For example, if the hunter want to know how much animal blood is needed in order to produce enough Vitae to feed an elder vampire, the hunter rolls Science + Energetic Theory [Vitae].<br /> <br /> While a theoretical understanding is all good and nice, the Energetic Theories also have a practical use. This use is two folded- the first is creating a device which works on supernatural energy instead of a mundane one. Examples are a car which works of Vitae, a computer which uses Mana or a phone which is charged by Essence. The second practical use is creating weapon which work on the certain supernatural energy. Those weapons (mostly guns, but some use swords or other cold weapons) always deal Lethal damage and ignore defense- and when they are used to attack their appropriate &quot;energy source&quot; (example, using a Source Gun against a witch) the weapon disrupt the energy of the target and makes the damage into Aggravated. An hunter may have a number of either functions equal to his dots in the Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T10:35:53-08:00","id":44979,"title":"","content":"so.. any ideas for the Union? For now I think they'll turn up to be something similar to the Dollars from Durarara!!, nut I'm open to suggestions :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T15:28:35-08:00","id":45176,"title":"","content":"The Union's biggest strength, as a whole, is its ability to compare notes. Most of that signal is obscured by a ton of noise, but it seems to me that their big catalysing event would come from comparing the right notes and identifying a widespread monster conspiracy that requires coordinated simultaneous action to overcome. Tactical necessity pushes the Union into greater cohesion, and it follows by becoming more organised rather than falling back into its former piecemeal state. It's not the kind of group that would invent an Endowment, so whatever it gets would logically be taken from the group it overcame. That implies some sort of magic or some sort of gadgetry.<br /> <br /> <i>If</i> they were to invent an Endowment themselves, I think it should be tied to their homebody aspect. Something that invokes the genius loci of the neighbourhood. Again, that's something that could be put together from compared notes on werewolves, witches, and others. And would probably count as a catalysing event in itself if it happened (though it would probably break the Union in half between those who adopted and rejected the technique - or maybe into thirds, those who adopt, those who reject but accept, and those who reject and count those who accept as witches).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:22:53-08:00","id":49937,"title":"","content":"<b>The Union</b><br /> <br /> The Union was a Tier 2 group with the mindset of a Tier 1 hunters. While they do work together and share their information, they are too independent, too individual. The very fact that such a group exist is an anomaly, something that shouldn't have happened. How that anomaly could evolve even further? How that group could attain the status of a conspiracy? This is ridiculous! Surly there was a need for a great and terrible disaster to gather them all together..<br /> <br /> Or that they simply got enough time.<br /> <br /> Look on the modern western world (and in many cases, even beyond that). Space and time became meaningless, as one could talk with people across the ocean and find information which was written thousands of years ago- and was uploaded to the net. Sure, other organizations has gained power from the evolution of the internet- but so does the Union. No the members needed to physically meet in order to work together. Their teamwork could have finally work from miles and miles away, and while most of the time they worked alone- in a matter of seconds they could be organized under a single purpose.<br /> <br /> The problem was, of course, that there was no one to organize them.<br /> <br /> And that was what have changed.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, all of the members of the Union has got a strange email. The email contained an application for any smartphone, although it could have also been installed in a computer, and it promised to allow the members to work better together by creating a private network safe from supernatural beings- and more, and its name was the HunterNet. The sender, which called itself Y, simply asked from the group to delete the mail afterward, to make sure that the only ones with the app will be the members of the Union. As you may imagine, not everyone has downloaded the app- but most of the younger members did, and with that things have changed.<br /> <br /> At first, the HunterNet was used simply for improve the teamwork of their members- but slowly, the Union discovered they weren't alone on the virtual space. Other hunters from all the world, all with the same ideology and methods, were also invited by Y. Suddenly, the Union discovered it wasn't alone in the World of Darkness- and that now it was truly united.<br /> <br /> Slowly and surely, more and more members of the Union has joined the HunterNet. While a member of the Union could add any person to the app, Y was the one to decide who will be approved and who will be denied. While the connection of hundreds (if not thousands!) of people was truly magnificent, the greatest use of the app was still on its way.<br /> <br /> One day, all the members of the Union discovered a message from Y- it was called a &quot;Challenge&quot;. There was a woman being chased by a psycho killer, and the Union had to stop it. Each member was asked if he would like to join the Challenge, and those who agreed will get points for doing so. Those who agreed to the Challenge has got a series of orders to fulfill- most of them were simple, like closing a certain door or starting the fire alarm. In ten minutes, all of the members who joined the Challenge got a message that the killer was captured, together with a photo of him taken by the police.<br /> <br /> And it didn't stopped there.<br /> <br /> After few more Challenges, the members of the Union discovered that they could spend points in order to present their own Challenges to their community. Y would decide if to approve the Challenge (which was always done quickly), and broke each Challenge to a series of orders. No one knows how Y knows exactly which orders to give to each hunter, but one thing is for sure- today, the Union has truly became one of the greatest powers in the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- you get access to the HunterNet endowment<br /> 000- same<br /> 00000- same<br /> <br /> <b>Endowment: HunterNet</b> (0-00000)<br /> The HunterNet is the special app given to each member of the Union. Unlike some other endowments, the HunterNet works in a more fluid way, making the connection between people into easier and more powerful- and through it, one can do great and terrible things, from finding information to proposing Challenges which could change the world.<br /> <br /> The HunterNet has two uses. The first is to search help through it- by entering what you wish to search after into the search engine (for example, &quot;how to kill a vampire&quot;), you can find people who knows how to help you. This is a regular Investigation roll, to which you add your dots at the HunterNet. Through it, you can either contact another hunter or searching for an article written by someone else in the conspiracy. You must choose what to search before rolling. Dramatic failure will lead you to either a wrong information or to someone who think he knows the solution to your problems- but he doesn't.<br /> <br /> The second use, however, is used in order to effect the real world- Challenges. Challenges are divided into 5 levels, each requires more points in order to be proposed. 1st level Challenges are used in order to save someone's life. 2nd leve Challenges are used in order to track down someone. 3rd level Challenges are used in order to steal something. 4th level Challenges are moved into kidnapping. 5th level Challenges are used based around changing something in the world- from bringing down a company to changing the government.<br /> <br /> Because of that, Challenges could be used in two ways- first, by completing a Challenge. This is purely a storyteller territory, in which the ST creates a Challenge for the players to fulfill, and each of them also gets a list of orders. Each order fulfilled gives the character a number of Gaming Points, and each order worth a number of Points equal to the level of the Challenge. That means that completing 3 orders of a 2nd level Challenge will give the character 6 Gaming Points. The hunter can refuse to a Challenge with no price- although refusing too many Challenges could be expressed at loosing Status.<br /> <br /> Once the character has enough Gaming Points, they can take a more active role in the Challenge and propose one. In order to propose a Challenge, one must have enough Gaming Points, with each Challenge level costs the Level*10 (so 10 points for 1st, 20 for 2nd, etc). After that, the player would have to roll a series of rolls which represent how many hunters agree to the Challenge, and how well are their performances. The first roll is made from HunterNet+ Status (Union)- [Challenge's Level]. Dramatic Failure means that the Challenge was accepted in such a bad way that the player lose a dot in Status (Union) (no less than 1). Extraordinary Success gives you +5 dices to your all other rolls in the Challenge.<br /> <br /> After that, the player needs to make a series of rolls which represent the fulfillment of orders- the number of rolls needed is [Challenge's Level]*5 (so 5 rolls for 1st, 10 for 2nd, etc). Each roll is made from HunterNet+ Manipulation, which represent the teamwork and how well they follow the orders given by Y. Each Failure removes a die from the next roll. Each Success gives another die to the next roll. Exceptional Success means that the next rolls gets +2 dies. Dramatic Failure means that the all process has fallen apart, and that the Challenge has failed as a regular Failure. If the last roll ends with a failure, the Challenge failed. If it was a Dramatic Failure, not only that it failed, but that you are blamed for it- and you get a -1 modifier for the next time you propose a challenge. A Success means, of course, that the Challenge worked. Exceptional Success means that not only it worked, but it worked so well that people remember it as something great and inspiring, and you get +2 dies for the next time you propose a Challenge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And with it, I've finished with the Core Compacts! next week- the controversial Witchfinders!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:04:22-08:00","id":55556,"title":"","content":"and so we start with Witchfinders!<br /> <br /> <b>Division VI</b><br /> <br /> Division VI is bound by the lies of a single person. Mister Jones has controlled for such a long time that he has started to see them as his &quot;personal pawns&quot;, an squad of assassins used in order to get rid of any political or otherwise rival in the complicated society of Panopticon. He weaved the illusions around his pawns so carefully, that no one among the compact has ever suspected that they were being used by the tricks of one of the reality deviants they by themselves hunted down. While the use of the Division has made Mister Jones into a very powerful person in his society, powerful people are simply bigger targets for those who stand lower in the social ladder- and in societies like Panopticon, this is never a good thing.<br /> <br /> All things have changed when the compact has stopped getting new orders from their contact men. No more they got any new equipment to use or new names to hunt with the equipment they already had. They have tried to make a contact with Panopticon in order to get new order and find out what has happened to Jones, but they didn't found anything. The searched for other groups which may deployed by the organization, but they came up empty handed again. It almost seemed like everything they knew was a lie...<br /> <br /> And than, Miss Jett has showed up.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, all of the cell leaders were contacted by the mysterious woman, who gathered them for a &quot;secret meeting&quot;. When they came, they found a fair, black haired woman who seemed to be around her late 30's. She told them that she is sorry for the delay in orders, and that bureaucracy has stopped her from getting involved earlier and tell them about the news. The reason for the lack of orders was that lately there was a shift in the command chain, and that Mister Jones has been moved to another department. Also, after some system changes and the success of the field project named as Division VI, it was decided to move the compact from the control of Panopticon into the care of a new, independent agency which is specialized in reality deviants and how to deal with them which worked without connections to the government, and as such gained a lot more freedom- Project: G.A.T.E.<br /> <br /> Miss Jett has also told them that new researches has discovered new information about the way reality deviants work and how their deeds effected the rise in world entropy. According to the research, the world needed to release a certain amount of entropy from time to time, a phenomena called as &quot;Paradox&quot; by the reality deviants. The agents of Division VI should still hunt down reality deviant for they generate too much entropy, but sometimes it is needed so they must follow G.A.T.E's directions about who to kill and who to spare. Also, the Division VI agents should sometimes hunt the manifestations of entropy themselves instead of the reality deviants- but only on certain times. G.A.T.E would also send them messages about when should they do so. Finally, G.A.T.E has developed a new, experimental equipment which uses the forces of entropy in order to help them to hunt down both the reality deviants and the manifestations. Also, she gave each of them he phone number and the contact details of other members of G.A.T.E members, so they won't have to suffer again from the same situation they experienced when the connection to Mister Jones was moved (&quot;so irresponsible for him to not let you know he was leaving&quot; she said &quot;at least he should had sending a farewell letter. How rude of him&quot;)<br /> <br /> While the equipment given by G.A.T.E wasn't that easy to be used at first, Division VI has quickly adapted to its new situation. Also, Miss Jet has also made contact with them regularly and contacted them with new groups which were &quot;lost in the bureaucracy&quot; of Panoptiocon and similar governmental agencies. Under the mantle of G.A.T.E, Division VI has steadily grown in power, and the communication between the compact itself and its sponsor has became better and better. Unlike Mister Jones, Miss Jett was a lot more reachable, and she also allowed them to meet other members of G.A.T.E. However, G.A.T.E and Division VI has became so powerful, that they have started to draw the attention of reality deviants, and so they couldn't have a permanent headquarters. Still, Miss Jett have always knew how to find the members of the Division and to equip them with the best their agency could make. In short, life have never been better for the Division- if only the nightmares made by their &quot;gifts&quot; from G.A.T.E would finally stop..<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- you get access to endowments: Paradox Technologies.<br /> 000- same<br /> 00000- you get Contacts for 4 dots to represent your connections with G.A.T.E<br /> <br /> <b>Endowments: Paradox Technologies</b> (0-00000, special)<br /> The so called &quot;Paradox Technologies&quot; are the strange equipment given to Division VI by G.A.T.E. According to Miss Jett, the Paradox Technologies are a special creation for they are the only thing in the world which can turn entropy into a fully useable force. Each of the devices made according to that process feeds upon the falling structure of the universe and covert it back into functional energy, so their very existence is good for the universe (which is a paradox- hence the name). However, their passive function is not enough in order to keep the world intact, and so Division VI must take a more active role, hunting down reality deviants who break the world too much and banishing being and phenomena which are made of entropy after they universe has released &quot;enough pressure&quot;. However, being so close to such a technology has some.. problems, for the presence of so much entropy may effect the user's mind.<br /> <br /> Each Paradox Technology is a bio-mechanical creation, made by synthesis phenomena from the broken voids of reality into a way which connect both our reality and a reality which works on a different laws of physics. The device works by drawing entropy and sending it to the other dimension, which is built to deal with so much entropy. Those bio- mechanical construct are not meant to be used physically- G.A.T.E actually forbid it literally- and they are meant to be built upon a physical item, from a weapon to a computer.<br /> <br /> There are two types of Paradox Technologies- the first is called Banisher, which works on reality deviants. The second is called Warder, which works on entropy manifestations. Each type is divided into different 1-5 dots, and the character can have 1 such device per dot in the Endowment. However, for each dot in Paradox Technology (both of them), the character suffer from a -1 modifier for Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Both types of Paradox Technologies have 4 uses- the first use is called &quot;entropy enhancement&quot;, in which the character adds the dots in the appropriate Paradox Technology to the rolls which involve the function of the device (shooting with a gun, using a computer, etc). Second, is the &quot;passive use&quot;, which during it the entropy enhancement stops working- but instead it allows the character to deal better with reality deviant and entropy manifestations. When the device is from the Banisher type, each reality deviant in the range of [Banisher dots] meters suffer from a penalty of -[Banisher dots] modifier to any roll which is connected to casting spells. The passive use of Warder gives the same penalty in the same range for ANY of the rolls made by an entropy manifestation.<br /> <br /> The third use, also called &quot;aggressive mode&quot;, works when both other functions are turned off and make the Paradox Function into a weapon which shoot invisible &quot;entropy blasts&quot; against the target which is found in the range. The user must tell the Paradox Technology who to shoot, for it was made to understand human speech and not to act without order. Any human hit by such blast suffer a Bashing damage. A corporal supernatural being (for Banisher) or spiritual being (for Warder) suffer from it a Lethal damage. Reality deviants (Banisher) or entropy manifestation (Warder) suffer from a an Aggravated damage by the appropriate Paradox Technology. The last use is &quot;self destruct&quot; in which the Paradox Technology destroys itself in order to create a certain effect. Banisher Technologies make a reality deviant in the range to suffer an automatic Paraodx, no matter what their Gnosis is, while Warder banish automatically any entropy manifestation back into the &quot;entropy world&quot; which is connected by Paradox Technology. However, making Paradox Technologies isn't cheap, and an agent must wait for a 6-[dots in Status] weeks until he'll get a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-29-2014, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T13:17:40-08:00","id":61020,"title":"","content":"<b>Keepers of the Source</b><br /> <br /> The Keepers has been divided into two different philosophies more or less since their beginning- one group has supported a pacifistic way of life, with trying to convince witches that draining the Source harmed the world. The other took things to their own hands, threading, beating and killing anyone who was even thinking about draining the sacred blood of Mother Earth. While divided, both sides are united around a single cause- protecting the sacred places from harm and stopping anyone who wishes to violate them. Unfortunately, both sides didn't had any effective ways to achieve that cause- the pacifists couldn't make the occultists to listen to the words of a &quot;group of ignorant sleepers&quot;, while the militant faction has just drawn fire to the compact- and they lacked the big guns in order to deal with their enemies.<br /> <br /> However, the Keepers had one advantage over the supernatural beings who dared to harm the Earth- their psychic sense, the ability to hear the screams of the Mother, the connection to her Sacred Blood. While that sense has allowed them to map the ley lines of all of San Fransisco. Slowly, more talented Dowsers has started to map more and more of the North America, which has granted them a better understand of how the blood of the Mother was flowing through the world. Slowly, they managed not only to track down the course in which the Source was moving through the earth, but also to guess where it was likely for a Source to be found and what effected its flowing. As their knowledge about the earth grew, they have started to attract the attention of some shady organizations who wished to buy or steal their information. While some of those were witches or other monsters, some were humans who either hunted down monsters or simply wished to use that knowledge for their own gain. That has made Karen Redgrove, the leader of the compact, to understand the terrible realization that it was only a matter of time before they'll be either absorbed by some other group or will be crushed down by a competitor. There was only one way to solve that problem- and it was to rise in power and become a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Were some compacts has risen to greatness by simply surviving or being in the right place and the right time, Karen wasn't the person to relay on random chances (witches had too much influence over it). No, this was a planned move, with Karen following each and every movement of her plan, which she shared with only few trusted members of the Dynasts. First, she needed money, for no grand organization could survive without financial support. That took some trainings, in which (by analyzing the compact's ley line maps) she used her understanding of the world's energy flow in order to find resources, like gems and precious metals. She was careful, however, for she didn't wished to harm the natural world (this was against anything she believed in), and this was way she didn't searched after things like oil and coal- sure, she could, but finding and selling those things won't help saving mother nature. The resources found by her specialized dowsers were than turned into fine jewellery or simply sold as they were for big companies. Sure, it may not be the most efficient way to gain money, but Karen didn't wished for a lot of money- just enough in order to advance her plans. Plus, thanks to their maps, the Keepers knew exactly were they should dig, which allowed them to gain a fine amount of money.<br /> <br /> Yet, the compact couldn't live upon raw materials forever, and this was were the second stage of the plan has started- Karen used the money she gained and invested it in alternative energy programs. While not all of them succeed, enough of them did, which has allowed her to gain some profit from her investments. When she had enough money, she has called a meeting with all of the members of the compact, telling them that they had enough time hiding in the shadows, and now it was time to move into the light. The Keepers should become a movement dedicated to protecting the Mother Earth, and while they can't tell everyone about the Source (they won't believe them) they can protect the mother in other ways.While some of the more militant members of the Keepers didn't agreed with the new direction, most of the Children of Gaia joined without thinking twice, which has forced the majority of the Hands to agree for the change- and while a few of them has left the Keepers, Karen knew they would. It was planned, after all.<br /> <br /> As a green movement, the Keepers has started to grow fast. Thanks for the permanent financial income from their dowsing talent and the investment in alternative energy projects, many other green organizations has joined their flag (when asked about their name, they simply said the the &quot;Source&quot; has represented Nature, for it was the source of all life). While the occult society of San Fransisco was suspicious about the move, most of them didn't gave it too much attention, for during that time the members of the Keepers has stopped bothering witches from using the &quot;sacred places&quot;, which made them think that the crazy hippies has finally gave up. That was also planned- a gambit. Sure, it hurt Karen to do so (literally), but she had to fool her enemies, else all of her plan will be crushed.<br /> <br /> Under their new guise, they have managed to gain even more financial support- after all, there were enough people who donated money in order to protect the planet. They have also started to absorb other green movements, which gave them the members they needed in order to gain influence and power. After a while, they didn't simply invested in green project, but have also started projects of their own, which allowed them to get even more money. While most of their new members didn't knew about the true agenda of the Keepers, those who were trusted enough were educated by the core members of the organization. However, rising in power was only one part of the plan- enriching their occult knowledge was the other part.<br /> <br /> Karen understood that in the same way that there could be an alternative energy for oil and coal, there could be an alternative way to use magic- one which wasn't built upon draining the sacred blood of the Mother. Once presented with the &quot;alternative Source use&quot;, witches won't have an excuse to drain Source- and even if they do have one, it won't be important, for what she was after was to convince the Keepers, not the witches, that other ways for Source-using do exist, and that if they do than witches have no real reason to drain the sacred blood of the mother. That will show the witches as the true villains, and make most of the Children to agree to use violence from time to time. Developing that technique was the true use for most of the money, but not all of it. Some was invested in gathering intelligence- the names of witches who had an high rank in the mundane society- together with every dirty secret they could find on them.<br /> <br /> The next part in her plan was a gamble. After developing the new Source using technique, Karen needed a symbol- an hero which will unite the organization. There was only such person who could fulfill that role- Starflower. It took her some time, but finally she managed to track Meredith down. While Meredith didn't wished to even meet with Karen, the new leader of the Keepers eventually managed to convince the founder to talk with her. During that conversation, Karen showed Meredith her new technique and told her that there was a way for the witches to finally stop abusing their power, and that she wished her to join the Keepers as a member to guide the movement in order to protect the world. While Meredith wasn't entirely convinced about the purity of Karen's words, the option of finally saving the world and making peace with the witches was too much for her to give up. And so, she joined- and Karen had only one more piece in her plan in order to protect the Keepers from harm.<br /> <br /> The last part was the loudest. In a week, Karen and Meredith worked together in order to teach all of the members of the not-longer-a-compact the &quot;Source friendly&quot; magic. While some were suspicious about it and thought that it may come from a dark origin, those who had the psychic sense told them that it truly was safe- the power was using source, but instead of stealing it from the world it simply moved through the user. Then, Karen told the members to use their new technique in order to protect themselves and any propriety of the Keepers from harm, so witches won't try to harm them after her finale move- using the movement's political power in order to reveal all of the corrupted witches' crimes she managed to dig up. The act has manged to deal some real harm to the witches' society while strengthening the Keepers' position in the wide majority of the population. That was the moment in which the Keepers have done history- and founded themselves as a true Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- you can spend merit dots on endowment: Green Magic<br /> 00- You get Resources for 2 dots<br /> 00000- You get Mentor for 3 dots<br /> <br /> <b>Endowment: Green Magic</b> (0- 00000)<br /> One doesn't need to drain the blood of Mother Earth in order work miracles. One can also simply ask. Mother Earth is generous, after all, and what other steal by force the Keepers get as a gift. Instead of draining Source like regular magic, Green Magic works naturally with the flow the ebb of the Source. The downside is that Green Magic works more slowly and must be planned carefully, but it is a small price to pay in order to protect the world from harm- or, at least, this is how the Keepers believe.<br /> <br /> In order to use Green Magic, the Keeper must first choose a single Gutter Magic Mystery (or Mage's spell), Which must be found either in play or by rolling Occult+ Investigation . The player can't choose a power which its rating is higher than his dots in Green Magic<br /> <br /> The next phase is based around the Dowser's own natural sense to the Source- where once the ability to hear the screams of Mother Earth belonged only for few, it is now the very base of their powers (meaning that Green Magic also serves as Unseen Sense: Source, although it comes into effect merit only when Green Magic's rating is equal to 2 dots). The player rolls (Green Magic)+ Wits in order to sense the movements of the Source, with Dramatic Failure means that the Dowser interpenetrate the movements of the Source wrongly and Exceptional Success gives +2 dices to all the next rolls of Green Magic. Thanks to that knowledge, the Dowser can make a map of the ley lines, which would allow him to use that energy naturally.<br /> <br /> After making the preparations, the Keeper must travel according the ley lines until he finds the place from where he could send his wish to Mother Earth. The target of the Green Magic must be found on the ley line's channel, which makes effecting moving targets an almost impossible task. After finding the right line, the Dowser spend a single point of Willpower in order to tune to the sacred blood of the Mother (in case of Dramatic Failure in the mapping, the point is wasted with no effect). Than, the player rolls (Green Magic)+ Intelligence and channel his wish trough the ley lines. Dramatic Failure means that somethings has backfired, and the character suffer from one level of bashing damage plus the pain from their Unseen Sense. Failure means that the willpower of the Dowser wasn't enough to work the spell. Success means that the spell happened just as the ritual meant it would. Exceptional Success also gives the character his lost Willpower point.<br /> <br /> While Green Magic can not create new rituals, if the Storyteller wishes he may allow the player to choose to mimic any kind of ritual magic (rites, ceremonies, blood sorcery and even the endowments of other, ritualistic conspiracies). Green Magic may not, however, effect the character herself- doing so will make the Dowser to contain Source in her own body, which would cause the effects of Dramatic Failure (pain and Bashing Damage). Effecting any other member of the Conspiracy is possible, yet it would make them suffer from the effects like they by themselves rolled Dramatic Failure- even if the effect means to be beneficial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:05:46-08:00","id":75149,"title":"","content":"Well, my mind is kinda blank for Spirit Slayers' compacts right now.. any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"htt